  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275040/assets/e4b9477517024d509134097c1964d830b5e0ba75fed2269717400e3ffb92d82b.png)\n\nWhat is the length of the semi-major axis of the ellipse given above?",
  "worked_solution": "The major axis is the longest diameter of the ellipse, which is the line segment bounded by the points $(2,1)$ and $(2,-4).$ So, the length of the major axis is $1-(-4)=5.$\n\nThe length of the semi-major axis is half the length of the major axis. So, the length of the semi-major axis is $\\frac{5}{2}=2.5.$",
